  "deduplicate_points": {
   "version": "0.1.0",
   "released": "2026-10-21",
   "changes": [
    {
     "kind": "minor",
     "description": "Two sources over one study area draw the same hospital twice, and a count of facilities is then wrong by however many of those there are. This compares records ACROSS sources and merges the pairs that agree, by the contracts of EPIAI RECORDLINK: blocking first, so pairs beyond a declared distance are never compared; binary contributions, so a similarity of 0.87 against a threshold of 0.88 contributes nothing rather than 0.87; and three classes rather than merge-or-not. A pair that passes both tests merges on its own. A pair that passes one WAITS FOR A PERSON and stays two records until somebody answers with a reason, which is pinned to a signature of the pair so that editing either record lapses the judgement. Missing never agrees with missing. Every threshold is a parameter and every parameter reaches the receipt. The review band is adjudicated in a dialog that shows both records side by side with every attribute each carries, the agreeing fields marked apart from the differing ones: the first version listed the pairs in the 292-pixel Inspector with two names and a distance, and the practitioner's answer was that it was unclear what was being adjudicated.",
