  "fill_interior_gaps": {
   "version": "0.1.0",
   "released": "2026-10-10",
   "changes": [
    {
     "kind": "initial",
     "description": "Each polygon replaced by its outer ring, so enclosed gaps become solid. This is isochrone's fillHoles as a step of its own, and it is what Advanced-1 NB03 does: Polygon(new_iso.exterior) at cell 64, the definition that produced the shapefiles NB04 reads. Cell 94 redefines the function to take a convex hull of multipart results and never calls it, which had earlier been mistaken for the operative infill. Takes no UTM zone, unlike the nine widgets that do: the input states the metric CRS its upstream used and this reads it, because a zone asked for twice can be answered twice. Gaps between separate polygons are untouched -- it fills enclosed space and does not join things up. The dangerous case governs itself through the port type: donut_geomask, where a hole is the privacy mechanism, emits points and cannot reach a polygons input. See docs/experiments/88-filling-interior-gaps.md."
    }
   ],
   "breaking": false,
   "migrationFrom": []
