     "kind": "initial",
     "description": "The smallest convex outline containing a set of points, computed in a metric CRS. Derived from the PHI case studies rather than proposed: Advanced-2 NB02 hulls its death locations to bound a Voronoi diagram and Advanced-1 NB03 hulls the reached network, and docs/research/john-snow-voronoi.md recorded that hull and buffer should not be hidden inside Voronoi. It is also the first of six primitives an isochrone composition needs, and the only one unblocked today. Refuses fewer than three located points and refuses collinear ones, because a line encloses nothing. Takes a UTM zone for the same reason five other widgets do — a layer cannot state the coordinate system it is in, which is D5's finding in experiment 40 and this makes six. Named with a stage verb under the taxonomy proposed in experiment 76: many points become one shape, which is summarising. See docs/experiments/80-convex-hull.md."
