  "travel_time": {
   "version": "0.1.0",
   "released": "2026-10-12",
   "changes": [
    {
     "kind": "baseline",
     "description": "Extracted from the retired access widget, which derived proxy minutes inside a nearest-neighbour search. A widget and not a knob on nearest, by the test experiment 107 derived: a minutes column changes every row for every consumer of the distances carrier, so the contract moves. And not a third value of the unit knob either -- metres to kilometres is a pure conversion while minutes is a MODEL, a straight-line distance walked at a constant speed, and putting a model behind a unit selector would present an assumption as a unit. The assumption is named in the receipt on every run. Reads each row unit rather than assuming kilometres, because a metre reading divided by metres-per-minute is right while a kilometre reading is wrong by a thousand. A row with no distance gains no minutes: a missing distance is not a travel time of zero."
    }
   ],
